# K03 NS-ROLES-3 / NS-ROLES-VIS (the author, 2026-10-07; semantics #declaration-visibility): `x: Foo` declares
# no field Foo; Foo, an ordinary named Structure, is not visible above its definition, so x is a named Structure
# of its own (with the free name Foo), no binding to Foo.  m, below Foo, reads Foo's field: exit 7 when it gives 4.
x: Foo
Foo:
    size_t: v 4U
end: Foo
fn: m () int
    if: Foo\v != 4U
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: m
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
